<p>I like that theory&#8230; I suppose the question that still remains is &quot;Why the bloody hell would they do that?&quot;, but perhaps the long-term containment plan is to slow or stop the growth of the thing by causing it to use up its nutrients on feeding and growing brain and bone tissue (brain tissue being metabolically expensive to maintain, and bone expensive to grow).</p>
<p>If that were the reason, though, I think it would be a better &quot;stinger&quot; at the end of the article to state that, if only obliquely. It feels like a satisfying-but-unpleasant justification for the whole thing, so I'm'a headcanon it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
